1
00:00:06,510 --> 00:00:08,050
(Space Rice Cake)

2
00:00:08,480 --> 00:00:10,980
(Space Rice Cake)

3
00:00:11,280 --> 00:00:14,050
(Year 2023)

4
00:00:14,050 --> 00:00:16,120
(Bali)

5
00:00:16,390 --> 00:00:20,060
(As always, Torong set a trap,)

6
00:00:21,060 --> 00:00:23,260
(and Mimi made a mistake.)

7
00:00:24,160 --> 00:00:26,900
(However, since the Earth Arcaders acted as a team,)

8
00:00:26,900 --> 00:00:29,830
(they took collective responsibility.)

9
00:00:30,000 --> 00:00:33,040
(And here's Torong's message to them.)

10
00:00:33,040 --> 00:00:37,610
(Guys, I hope you're excited about working at a rice cake shop.)

11
00:00:37,740 --> 00:00:39,840
(They faced karma that could catch up with them at anytime.)

12
00:00:39,980 --> 00:00:42,110
There's something we really want to try.

13
00:00:42,110 --> 00:00:43,650
And we think that Director Ye Seul is the only one...

14
00:00:43,650 --> 00:00:45,680
- who can execute it perfectly.
- That's right.

15
00:00:46,420 --> 00:00:47,620
We'll get a really long garaetteok.

16
00:00:47,620 --> 00:00:49,150
- You see, I'm 175cm tall.
- Right.

17
00:00:49,150 --> 00:00:50,560
We'll make tteokbokki with a 175cm-long piece of garaetteok...

18
00:00:50,560 --> 00:00:51,760
and serve it in the shape of poop, coiled up like this.

19
00:00:51,760 --> 00:00:53,830
- Yu Jin will cut it into pieces...
- "Hello."

20
00:00:53,830 --> 00:00:55,290
- in front of our customers.
- Oh, she'll serve it to customers?

21
00:00:55,290 --> 00:00:56,360
- That's right.
- Yes, she'll serve it.

22
00:00:56,360 --> 00:00:58,330
Eun Ji can perform some numbers from "Rebecca," "Kinky Boots,"

23
00:00:58,330 --> 00:01:00,300
and "Mamma Mia!" What else can you do, Eun Ji?

24
00:01:00,300 --> 00:01:01,430
- "Seopyeonje."
- Right, "Seopyeonje."

25
00:01:01,430 --> 00:01:02,700
- "Seopyeonje?"
- She can do everything...

26
00:01:02,830 --> 00:01:05,000
- including waiting tables.
- I can work in the kitchen too.

27
00:01:05,000 --> 00:01:06,810
- She can work in the kitchen too.
- I can do that.

28
00:01:06,810 --> 00:01:07,910
- She can handle the kitchen work.
- Yes.

29
00:01:07,910 --> 00:01:10,240
And Mimi will make shaved ice, giving it some weird name.

30
00:01:10,840 --> 00:01:12,440
- She'll handle the desserts.
- I'll make the desserts.

31
00:01:12,440 --> 00:01:13,550
What do you think of our plan?

32
00:01:13,550 --> 00:01:14,680
When are we going to do this?

33
00:01:14,680 --> 00:01:16,710
- Let's set the date here and now.
- Tell us when you're available.

34
00:01:16,710 --> 00:01:17,820
Let's set the date.

35
00:01:17,820 --> 00:01:20,120
(They volunteered to take the penalty.)

36
00:01:20,420 --> 00:01:22,820
(However...)

37
00:01:22,820 --> 00:01:23,890
I'm not doing this!

38
00:01:23,890 --> 00:01:25,360
Wait. Hold on a second.

39
00:01:25,560 --> 00:01:26,960
Let's go on strike.

40
00:01:26,960 --> 00:01:28,860
- Hey, come on.
- Let's go on strike.

41
00:01:28,960 --> 00:01:30,200
- Hey.
- Why?

42
00:01:30,200 --> 00:01:31,200
- Let's go on strike!
- What's the matter?

43
00:01:31,200 --> 00:01:32,200
- What's wrong?
- Young Ji was doing it...

44
00:01:32,200 --> 00:01:34,670
- You asked us to send you...
- That doesn't matter now!

45
00:01:35,730 --> 00:01:37,200
(It all started two months ago.)

46
00:01:37,200 --> 00:01:39,670
Please try to understand us.

47
00:01:39,670 --> 00:01:41,610
She says she's craving rice cake.

48
00:01:41,810 --> 00:01:43,340
(Hello, everyone. Have you been well?)

49
00:01:43,340 --> 00:01:45,210
(The launch of Space Rice Cake's 1st Earth location is coming soon.)

50
00:01:45,210 --> 00:01:46,380
(Before you start working there, a contest will be held...)

51
00:01:46,380 --> 00:01:47,380
(to select the head chef of Space Rice Cake's 1st Earth location.)

52
00:01:47,380 --> 00:01:50,280
(A contest will be held to recruit a competent, talented chef.)

53
00:01:50,280 --> 00:01:51,780
(Before you start working there, a contest will be held...)

54
00:01:51,780 --> 00:01:53,250
(to select the head chef of Space Rice Cake's 1st Earth location.)

55
00:01:53,250 --> 00:01:54,450
(Prepare a rice cake recipe that suits Space Rice Cake's vision.)

56
00:01:54,450 --> 00:01:55,450
(Criteria, Taste: 40 percent, creativity: 40, profitability: 20)

57
00:01:55,450 --> 00:01:57,490
(The criteria are quite detailed for such a small contest.)

58
00:01:57,490 --> 00:01:58,990
(An Yu Jin: Oh, my!)

59
00:01:58,990 --> 00:02:01,030
(Lee Young Ji: Oh, my gosh! That should be me.)

60
00:02:01,030 --> 00:02:02,960
(Lee Young Ji: Bhut Jolokia, the world's spiciest chili)

61
00:02:02,960 --> 00:02:04,360
(Can I use this for my dish?)

62
00:02:04,360 --> 00:02:07,730
(One of the contestants makes a terrifying proposal.)

63
00:02:07,730 --> 00:02:08,830
(Lee Eun Ji: I'm dying to become the head chef.)

64
00:02:08,830 --> 00:02:10,370
(An Yu Jin: I practically crushed Young Ji. Is this even necessary?)

65
00:02:10,370 --> 00:02:11,400
(Provoking)

66
00:02:11,400 --> 00:02:12,870
(Lee Young Ji: That's funny. What a joke.)

67
00:02:12,870 --> 00:02:16,040
(A fierce battle of wits has broken out here for some reason.)

68
00:02:16,040 --> 00:02:17,680
(Mimi: I'm excited. My heart is pounding.)

69
00:02:17,680 --> 00:02:20,040
(Meanwhile, a hidden master stays calm.)

70
00:02:20,040 --> 00:02:21,650
(Eun Ji: I want to be the Monkfish Beast of "Earth Arcade.")

71
00:02:21,650 --> 00:02:23,880
(Lee Young Ji: I'll make you regret it. Just wait and see.)

72
00:02:23,880 --> 00:02:25,920
(I'll be the Hardheaded Chef.)

73
00:02:26,180 --> 00:02:29,450
(So they announced the appearance of the impersonators of famous chefs.)

74
00:02:29,550 --> 00:02:31,960
(The day of the contest)

75
00:02:32,320 --> 00:02:34,130
- Oh, boy.
- Gosh. What is going on?

76
00:02:34,130 --> 00:02:35,230
Gosh, seriously.

77
00:02:37,160 --> 00:02:39,430
Come on. Don't do things like this.

78
00:02:39,430 --> 00:02:40,970
(The first contestant is wearing vivid colors.)

79
00:02:41,230 --> 00:02:42,570
Is this what you wanted to do?

80
00:02:43,370 --> 00:02:44,400
- Gosh.
- Hello.

81
00:02:45,200 --> 00:02:46,640
Hello. It's nice to meet you all.

82
00:02:48,270 --> 00:02:50,210
- Oh, dear. I'm tired.
- Who are you?

83
00:02:50,210 --> 00:02:52,280
- I'm the head of...
- Who are you?

84
00:02:52,280 --> 00:02:53,950
I'm the head of a women's association.

85
00:02:54,210 --> 00:02:56,610
I can't look in Director Yeong Seok's direction...

86
00:02:56,610 --> 00:02:58,180
because I'm carrying heavy stuff on top of my head.

87
00:02:58,580 --> 00:03:00,350
- Hello.
- Put that down for now.

88
00:03:00,350 --> 00:03:01,420
Dear me.

89
00:03:02,050 --> 00:03:03,920
- We didn't give you a dress code.
- Pardon?

90
00:03:03,920 --> 00:03:05,890
We didn't give you a dress code. Then why...

91
00:03:05,890 --> 00:03:07,490
- You didn't give us a dress code?
- No.

92
00:03:07,560 --> 00:03:08,930
We didn't ask you to come in character like this.

93
00:03:08,930 --> 00:03:10,090
We simply asked you to show up.

94
00:03:10,090 --> 00:03:11,900
I didn't come in character. This is how I usually dress.

95
00:03:11,900 --> 00:03:13,570
- So you usually...
- This is how I always look.

96
00:03:13,700 --> 00:03:15,670
I've been dressing like this for the whole month.

97
00:03:15,670 --> 00:03:17,270
I made so much tteokbokki...

98
00:03:17,270 --> 00:03:19,540
that I don't even want to look at it now.

99
00:03:19,900 --> 00:03:22,240
- Am I the 1st to come?
- Yes, you're the 1st to come.

100
00:03:22,240 --> 00:03:23,580
I was carrying all this on my head,

101
00:03:23,580 --> 00:03:25,080
and Yu Jin held the elevator...

102
00:03:25,080 --> 00:03:26,310
and wouldn't let me go up.

103
00:03:26,310 --> 00:03:28,750
I was forced to carry this heavy basket on my head for a while.

104
00:03:28,750 --> 00:03:30,180
I thought my skull was going to crack.

105
00:03:30,380 --> 00:03:31,520
Why hasn't she come yet?

106
00:03:31,680 --> 00:03:32,850
- You mean, Yu Jin?
- Yes.

107
00:03:32,950 --> 00:03:34,120
She's gone to get some ingredients.

108
00:03:34,120 --> 00:03:36,220
She asked me if I had olive oil this morning...

109
00:03:36,220 --> 00:03:37,560
when we were going to compete against each other.

110
00:03:38,060 --> 00:03:39,660
I'm sorry, but I should go up.

111
00:03:39,660 --> 00:03:40,990
My head feels so heavy with this basket.

112
00:03:41,330 --> 00:03:42,360
- But...
- Look at my hair.

113
00:03:42,360 --> 00:03:43,360
I dyed my hair the color of tteokbokki.

114
00:03:43,360 --> 00:03:44,860
(Her hair looks perfect for the time, place, and occasion.)

115
00:03:44,860 --> 00:03:45,860
- Well...
- The color of tteokbokki.

116
00:03:45,860 --> 00:03:47,130
- The tone of your voice...
- Yes?

117
00:03:47,570 --> 00:03:49,370
- has changed a lot.
- What do you mean?

118
00:03:49,570 --> 00:03:50,870
Just think about the profitability.

119
00:03:51,070 --> 00:03:52,540
There's no way a person looking like this...

120
00:03:52,540 --> 00:03:53,870
makes bad tteokbokki.

121
00:03:54,440 --> 00:03:56,440
- A concept really matters nowadays.
- Exactly.

122
00:03:56,440 --> 00:03:58,040
I prepared myself so thoroughly as a contestant.

123
00:03:58,440 --> 00:03:59,880
You should be grateful as the director of the show.

124
00:03:59,880 --> 00:04:01,510
- Hello, everyone.
- She startled me.

125
00:04:01,510 --> 00:04:04,080
- Oh, she... Hey, be careful.
- Can somebody open the door for me?

126
00:04:04,080 --> 00:04:05,080
(Struggling)

127
00:04:05,680 --> 00:04:08,220
(The second contestant enters, staggering.)

128
00:04:08,790 --> 00:04:09,920
- What?
- Hello.

129
00:04:10,320 --> 00:04:12,220
- Hey...
- She came in character too.

130
00:04:12,490 --> 00:04:14,660
I am Mi Geum, not Jang Geum.

131
00:04:14,660 --> 00:04:15,660
- Hold on a second.
- You may hope

132
00:04:15,660 --> 00:04:17,730
- Our concepts are so different.
- He comes

133
00:04:17,730 --> 00:04:19,930
- But he might not - Look at you. My goodness.

134
00:04:20,230 --> 00:04:21,370
- Oh, my. You look...
- Exactly.

135
00:04:21,370 --> 00:04:22,870
- Our concepts are so different.
- What are you...

136
00:04:22,870 --> 00:04:24,870
What is this? What are you dressed as?

137
00:04:25,170 --> 00:04:26,800
Wait. Who is that?

138
00:04:26,800 --> 00:04:28,670
- Another one has come.
- Each of us...

139
00:04:28,670 --> 00:04:30,640
She's the one who looks like a newlywed bride.

140
00:04:30,640 --> 00:04:32,910
- Look at her. My goodness.
- You're like a survival contestant.

141
00:04:32,910 --> 00:04:34,580
- I went for Cheongdam-dong style.
- Hello.

142
00:04:35,250 --> 00:04:36,410
Come on, Young Ji.

143
00:04:36,710 --> 00:04:37,850
You could've given me some tips...

144
00:04:37,850 --> 00:04:39,380
- on a contest like this?
- You see...

145
00:04:39,550 --> 00:04:41,550
She and I talked all day today via messages.

146
00:04:41,550 --> 00:04:43,250
But she didn't tell me anything about what she would do today.

147
00:04:44,020 --> 00:04:45,690
- You know that's how she is.
- That's right.

148
00:04:45,690 --> 00:04:47,430
- She's built for a contest.
- Mimi.

149
00:04:47,430 --> 00:04:48,430
What are these?

150
00:04:48,430 --> 00:04:50,130
- Did you two buy these together?
- I put all my stuff in here.

151
00:04:50,260 --> 00:04:52,360
- This is mine, and that's hers.
- Let's not share what we brought.

152
00:04:52,460 --> 00:04:53,730
Okay. Should we be wary of each other?

153
00:04:53,730 --> 00:04:54,730
- Yes, of course.
- Okay.

154
00:04:54,730 --> 00:04:57,500
I can already see right through her plan. The plan of this lady.

155
00:04:57,500 --> 00:04:59,600
- Mini sausages?
- I already got the feeling.

156
00:04:59,600 --> 00:05:00,610
What's my plan? Tell me.

157
00:05:00,610 --> 00:05:02,710
Obviously, you're planning to make Dubai chewy cookie, butter tteok,

158
00:05:02,710 --> 00:05:05,910
or some dessert that went out of fashion like 4,000 years ago.

159
00:05:05,910 --> 00:05:07,480
Four thousand years ago?

160
00:05:07,750 --> 00:05:09,250
- Your job is...
- Just wait and see.

161
00:05:09,250 --> 00:05:10,550
to serve the food I make...

162
00:05:10,850 --> 00:05:13,750
- to the customers.
- What are you going to make?

163
00:05:13,850 --> 00:05:15,850
- Move! You wash the dishes.
- Will you just mix everything?

164
00:05:16,290 --> 00:05:17,360
Mimi, you...

165
00:05:17,360 --> 00:05:18,660
(She has the face for doing the dishes.)

166
00:05:18,660 --> 00:05:20,760
She stands out too much outside.

167
00:05:20,760 --> 00:05:22,960
People are waiting downstairs because of you.

168
00:05:23,230 --> 00:05:24,660
- People are waiting?
- They all recognized you.

169
00:05:24,660 --> 00:05:26,430
- It's like a fan event.
- I look like a superstar.

170
00:05:27,630 --> 00:05:29,270
- I have that vibe.
- That's true.

171
00:05:29,270 --> 00:05:31,570
She's only wearing a necklace... She's not wearing bracelets.

172
00:05:31,570 --> 00:05:32,670
- That's right.
- What?

173
00:05:32,770 --> 00:05:33,970
- There's no way she's okay with it.
- She always wears bracelets.

174
00:05:33,970 --> 00:05:35,210
Mimi, you're so cool.

175
00:05:35,210 --> 00:05:36,510
- I stripped off all my accessories.
- Why did you do that?

176
00:05:36,510 --> 00:05:37,640
- I guess you sold them all.
- I took off all my rings.

177
00:05:37,640 --> 00:05:38,640
- Sorry?
- You sold them all.

178
00:05:38,640 --> 00:05:40,910
For today's contest, I took them off...

179
00:05:40,910 --> 00:05:42,650
- with determination.
- Really?

180
00:05:42,750 --> 00:05:43,820
- But actually, - Because you'd be cooking?

181
00:05:43,820 --> 00:05:45,750
I feel a little less confident right now.

182
00:05:46,050 --> 00:05:47,790
- Without my... I'm anxious.
- Because you're not wearing them?

183
00:05:47,790 --> 00:05:49,890
- I have separation anxiety.
- So you still have them.

184
00:05:49,890 --> 00:05:50,960
- You just took them off.
- That's right.

185
00:05:50,960 --> 00:05:52,260
- For today's contest?
- Yes.

186
00:05:52,260 --> 00:05:53,260
She wants to become the head chef.

187
00:05:53,260 --> 00:05:56,190
I didn't want my accessories to get in the way of my cooking.

188
00:05:56,190 --> 00:05:58,000
- You seem like a stranger.
- Exactly. I feel the same way.

189
00:05:58,000 --> 00:06:00,360
- I feel weird myself too.
- You seem like a stranger.

190
00:06:00,360 --> 00:06:01,730
Yu Jin, what's your concept?

191
00:06:01,730 --> 00:06:03,000
- I...
- An idol singer.

192
00:06:03,530 --> 00:06:05,240
(Giggling)

193
00:06:05,240 --> 00:06:07,440
- My goal to achieve on this show...
- Yes?

194
00:06:07,440 --> 00:06:08,470
is to be cute.

195
00:06:10,140 --> 00:06:12,440
- That's irrelevant to your food.
- Yu Jin.

196
00:06:12,780 --> 00:06:13,780
That has nothing to do with your food.

197
00:06:13,780 --> 00:06:14,950
- Yu Jin, you look...
- But you should go for it.

198
00:06:14,950 --> 00:06:17,380
- Sorry, but you're on a food show.
- I think it's a vintage style.

199
00:06:17,480 --> 00:06:19,280
We're not holding a fan event here.

200
00:06:19,280 --> 00:06:21,390
- I'll do the dishes looking cute.
- Even when you do the dishes?

201
00:06:21,390 --> 00:06:22,890
- Wearing pretty gloves?
- I'll serve food looking cute.

202
00:06:23,550 --> 00:06:24,690
- That's why...
- That's amazing.

203
00:06:24,690 --> 00:06:27,260
I'm wearing this apron with a rabbit on it.

204
00:06:28,030 --> 00:06:29,190
- I specially picked this apron.
- I see.

205
00:06:29,190 --> 00:06:31,430
So that's how you're going to win over the heads of the show?

206
00:06:31,830 --> 00:06:33,560
- It's the Torong special theme.
- Okay.

207
00:06:33,560 --> 00:06:34,930
- It's totally irrelevant...
- I'll put on my apron too.

208
00:06:34,930 --> 00:06:37,030
- to food.
- I'll be cute.

209
00:06:37,270 --> 00:06:39,670
It's hard to get used to this side of Yu Jin since it's been a while...

210
00:06:39,670 --> 00:06:41,540
She came up with this idea that's totally irrelevant to food.

211
00:06:41,540 --> 00:06:43,040
You think it's easy to get used to this side of you?

212
00:06:43,640 --> 00:06:45,840
- You're the strangest one here.
- You look like a village head.

213
00:06:45,840 --> 00:06:47,180
- What?
- Oh, gosh. She startled me.

214
00:06:47,180 --> 00:06:48,180
- Eun Ji.
- Eun Ji.

215
00:06:48,180 --> 00:06:49,650
Eun Ji, at least you're dressed normally.

216
00:06:49,650 --> 00:06:50,880
- Right. She's dressed normally.
- I'm relieved.

217
00:06:51,080 --> 00:06:53,220
I thought you might dress up, which made me nervous.

218
00:06:53,220 --> 00:06:55,320
Eun Ji, why are you looking embarrassed?

219
00:06:55,320 --> 00:06:57,160
I'm sorry, but will there be a play performed here?

220
00:06:59,090 --> 00:07:02,830
I wasn't told that we were going to perform...

221
00:07:02,830 --> 00:07:04,530
a play here.

222
00:07:04,530 --> 00:07:05,930
- Then what...
- Today, I...

223
00:07:05,930 --> 00:07:08,400
What is this actress doing here?

224
00:07:08,400 --> 00:07:10,230
- I wanted to be the head chef.
- I see.

225
00:07:10,230 --> 00:07:11,940
She's absolutely burning with ambition to take that spot.

226
00:07:11,940 --> 00:07:13,370
Wait. Hold on.

227
00:07:13,370 --> 00:07:15,770
I should've prepared a special outfit like she did.

228
00:07:15,770 --> 00:07:17,680
- We didn't ask her to do that.
- Exactly. Creativity...

229
00:07:17,680 --> 00:07:19,680
- is one of the criteria.
- It was all her idea.

230
00:07:19,910 --> 00:07:20,910
(Acting arrogant)

231
00:07:20,910 --> 00:07:24,580
Young Ji, you looked so cool at your concert. What's this?

232
00:07:24,580 --> 00:07:25,980
Don't I look cool now?

233
00:07:26,380 --> 00:07:27,890
I'm dedicated to my concept.

234
00:07:27,890 --> 00:07:29,020
- You do look pretty.
- Right.

235
00:07:29,020 --> 00:07:30,120
- Thank you.
- You're welcome.

236
00:07:30,250 --> 00:07:31,920
- I'm a little worried right now.
- About what?

237
00:07:31,920 --> 00:07:34,130
I'm just as nervous as I was before the comedian audition.

238
00:07:34,130 --> 00:07:35,630
- Why do you always...
- Every night,

239
00:07:35,630 --> 00:07:37,460
- I had a nightmare.
- Me too.

240
