473
00:15:28,330 --> 00:15:29,870
We'll practically serve a queen.

474
00:15:29,870 --> 00:15:31,300
- My goodness.
- I understand.

475
00:15:31,300 --> 00:15:32,500
- We'll have to bathe you...
- We'll have to serve her.

476
00:15:32,500 --> 00:15:33,700
- and put socks on you.
- Put socks on me.

477
00:15:33,700 --> 00:15:35,740
- Then pay your respects to me.
- We'll have to serve you.

478
00:15:35,740 --> 00:15:37,680
- Yes. You'll be like my servants.
- We'll have to serve her.

479
00:15:37,680 --> 00:15:38,740
(While discussing the misconceived privilege of the head chef...)

480
00:15:40,110 --> 00:15:41,680
They don't seem tense at all.

481
00:15:43,880 --> 00:15:44,950
That really bothers me.

482
00:15:47,120 --> 00:15:48,650
They don't seem to be ready to cook.

483
00:15:49,890 --> 00:15:52,860
(Someone is keeping a shrewd eye on them.)

484
00:15:52,960 --> 00:15:54,990
I have a question.

485
00:15:54,990 --> 00:15:57,390
- Who are the judges?
- Right. I'm curious about that too.

486
00:15:57,660 --> 00:16:00,060
(Finally, they're asking about him.)

487
00:16:00,060 --> 00:16:02,400
Then we're going to introduce you to the judge.

488
00:16:02,400 --> 00:16:03,670
- All right.
- I don't want to see.

489
00:16:03,670 --> 00:16:04,940
- I'm nervous.
- I'll be too nervous.

490
00:16:04,940 --> 00:16:06,300
- Please come in.
- What?

491
00:16:06,300 --> 00:16:07,400
Are we going to cook in front of the judge?

492
00:16:07,400 --> 00:16:09,370
- Judge.
- Torong.

493
00:16:09,940 --> 00:16:11,540
- Oh, it's Torong.
- I knew it.

494
00:16:11,540 --> 00:16:14,080
- Isn't he Chef Ahn Sung Jae?
- Chef Ahn Sung Jae?

495
00:16:14,080 --> 00:16:16,080
That's how Chef Ahn Sung Jae dresses all the time.

496
00:16:16,080 --> 00:16:17,280
(Torong is sharply dressed in a formal suit.)

497
00:16:17,510 --> 00:16:18,580
What do we do?

498
00:16:18,850 --> 00:16:20,320
- Why?
- Why?

499
00:16:21,020 --> 00:16:22,350
Oh, there must be someone else behind Torong.

500
00:16:22,350 --> 00:16:24,460
- Someone else is coming?
- Torong isn't the judge.

501
00:16:24,720 --> 00:16:27,790
No way. This is unfair. This is wrong.

502
00:16:28,190 --> 00:16:29,490
(Exclaiming in disapproval)

503
00:16:29,690 --> 00:16:31,230
(This is unfair! This is wrong!)

504
00:16:31,900 --> 00:16:34,930
No way. This is unfair. This is wrong.

505
00:16:35,130 --> 00:16:36,730
- No, it's not like that.
- This is unfair.

506
00:16:37,130 --> 00:16:39,440
- I'm sorry, but please leave.
- This is unfair.

507
00:16:39,540 --> 00:16:42,070
- Why?
- We need you to leave now.

508
00:16:42,070 --> 00:16:44,810
- Leave. Let's find another judge.
- Why?

509
00:16:44,810 --> 00:16:46,210
- Let's find another judge.
- I'm not doing this.

510
00:16:46,210 --> 00:16:48,710
- Why?
- We'll find another one. Leave.

511
00:16:48,710 --> 00:16:50,180
- He needs to leave.
- Why?

512
00:16:50,180 --> 00:16:52,980
- We're not doing this.
- We met him not long ago.

513
00:16:52,980 --> 00:16:54,690
- It's not what you're thinking.
- I'm not doing this.

514
00:16:54,690 --> 00:16:56,950
- This isn't right.
- We really didn't plan this.

515
00:16:56,950 --> 00:16:58,590
- We just ate together.
- We're not behind this.

516
00:16:58,590 --> 00:16:59,890
- You treat your guest like this?
- We just ate together.

517
00:17:00,190 --> 00:17:02,190
- Please come and sit down.
- Okay.

518
00:17:02,290 --> 00:17:03,290
- My goodness.
- Hello.

519
00:17:03,290 --> 00:17:05,000
- This isn't fair.
- This is...

520
00:17:05,000 --> 00:17:07,300
- Please sit here.
- Should I sit down?

521
00:17:07,300 --> 00:17:08,530
- Please sit down for now.
- Should I sit down?

522
00:17:08,630 --> 00:17:09,630
(Exclaiming in disapproval)

523
00:17:09,870 --> 00:17:11,970
- Hello, everyone.
- Mimi, come here.

524
00:17:11,970 --> 00:17:13,700
Is it because I'm not the one you were expecting to see?

525
00:17:13,870 --> 00:17:14,970
(Everyone is seated now.)

526
00:17:15,070 --> 00:17:16,540
- We all know who you are, - Yes?

527
00:17:16,540 --> 00:17:18,010
but can you please introduce yourself to the viewers?

528
00:17:18,010 --> 00:17:19,680
- Me? Which camera should I look at?
- Yes.

529
00:17:19,680 --> 00:17:22,410
- Oh, my. But we don't do that here.
- Is that so?

530
00:17:22,780 --> 00:17:25,050
- You can look at Young Ji.
- Look at Young Ji.

531
00:17:25,150 --> 00:17:26,280
I don't feel so comfortable... Her outfit...

532
00:17:26,480 --> 00:17:29,220
- She has a camera here.
- Oh, really?

533
00:17:29,220 --> 00:17:30,250
- Young Ji has a camera here.
- Hello.

534
00:17:30,250 --> 00:17:31,990
I'm Manager Kwon Sung Jun from the Menu Development Team...

535
00:17:31,990 --> 00:17:33,060
of the head office.

536
00:17:33,060 --> 00:17:34,590
Oh, my. That's crazy.

537
00:17:34,930 --> 00:17:37,190
When did you plant the idea of this universe in his head?

538
00:17:37,530 --> 00:17:39,500
I perfectly understand this universe.

539
00:17:39,600 --> 00:17:41,830
- You're from the head office.
- Yes, I'm from the head office.

540
00:17:41,830 --> 00:17:43,530
- This is my first time seeing you.
- Where is this head office?

541
00:17:43,530 --> 00:17:44,800
You mean, the head office of egg is coming?

542
00:17:45,370 --> 00:17:47,670
- No, they said it was somewhere...
- Then what?

543
00:17:47,670 --> 00:17:49,870
- Where is it?
- Where?

544
00:17:49,870 --> 00:17:51,880
- Where is it?
- They said it was on the Moon.

545
00:17:52,040 --> 00:17:53,180
(The basic "Earth Arcade" knowledge test is not easy.)

546
00:17:53,180 --> 00:17:54,240
Isn't it on the Moon?

547
00:17:54,340 --> 00:17:56,180
- It is on the Moon.
- Yes.

548
00:17:56,180 --> 00:17:58,580
Did they tell you where our restaurant will be?

549
00:17:58,580 --> 00:17:59,580
I don't know that.

550
00:18:00,650 --> 00:18:03,820
Didn't the head office approve the opening of this branch?

551
00:18:04,120 --> 00:18:05,690
- That's what I heard.
- Okay.

552
00:18:06,160 --> 00:18:08,030
- Right. I think that's right.
- Exactly.

553
00:18:08,030 --> 00:18:09,290
- I have a question.
- Go ahead.

554
00:18:09,290 --> 00:18:11,330
When did you meet these two?

555
00:18:11,330 --> 00:18:13,130
I really believe that this is my first time meeting him.

556
00:18:13,130 --> 00:18:14,800
- But this is...
- Please tell us the truth.

557
00:18:14,800 --> 00:18:16,000
- We have an issue with fairness.
- That's right.

558
00:18:16,000 --> 00:18:17,030
- This is...
- What's the problem?

559
00:18:17,030 --> 00:18:20,000
Did you secretly give them a private cooking lesson?

560
00:18:20,270 --> 00:18:21,270
A private lesson?

561
00:18:22,170 --> 00:18:23,310
I didn't give them a private lesson. That's for sure.

562
00:18:23,310 --> 00:18:25,040
- What do you mean?
- What are you not sure about?

563
00:18:25,040 --> 00:18:27,180
- We got no help from you.
- I think he did something.

564
00:18:27,180 --> 00:18:28,610
- You gave us nothing.
- I think he did something.

565
00:18:28,850 --> 00:18:30,880
- No, I had no idea.
- That's right.

566
00:18:30,880 --> 00:18:32,350
- They came to my restaurant.
- I see.

567
00:18:33,320 --> 00:18:35,820
I heard them gossiping about you guys.

568
00:18:36,220 --> 00:18:37,650
- Gossiping?
- Gossiping?

569
00:18:37,650 --> 00:18:38,960
They backbit?

570
00:18:38,960 --> 00:18:41,260
- They backbit a little bit...
- They backbit us.

571
00:18:41,260 --> 00:18:42,930
- I'm sure...
- But it's what we do all the time.

572
00:18:43,460 --> 00:18:45,160
We all do that.

573
00:18:45,260 --> 00:18:47,200
- I'm sorry, but...
- That's not true.

574
00:18:47,200 --> 00:18:49,370
- I'm disappointed in you.
- Young Ji would do that.

575
00:18:49,700 --> 00:18:51,770
- But did Yu Jin backbite us too?
- No, I didn't.

576
00:18:51,770 --> 00:18:53,270
Yu Jin did a bit more than Young Ji did.

577
00:18:53,540 --> 00:18:55,070
(Yu Jin was the one who went harder with the backbiting.)

578
00:18:55,070 --> 00:18:58,140
I'm not doing this. That just ruined our friendship and everything.

579
00:18:58,140 --> 00:18:59,740
- This is absurd.
- May I ask you something?

580
00:18:59,740 --> 00:19:01,850
Did they backbite the other cast members or the staff?

581
00:19:01,850 --> 00:19:02,910
That's an important point.

582
00:19:02,910 --> 00:19:03,980
We probably did both. I don't remember.

583
00:19:03,980 --> 00:19:06,150
I'm not supposed to leak customer information...

584
00:19:06,150 --> 00:19:07,220
to outsiders...

585
00:19:07,220 --> 00:19:08,920
- But you already did it.
- You already did it.

586
00:19:09,250 --> 00:19:11,360
- Just give us a general idea.
- If I put it simply, she talked...

587
00:19:11,660 --> 00:19:13,990
- Okay, let's fight today.
- about the production crew.

588
00:19:14,390 --> 00:19:16,790
If you don't tell them exactly what happened,

589
00:19:16,790 --> 00:19:18,300
- there could be misunderstandings.
- Should I tell them?

590
00:19:18,300 --> 00:19:19,400
- Be specific.
- Are you okay with that?

591
00:19:19,400 --> 00:19:21,530
Yes, I'm okay with it. I don't mind.

592
00:19:21,670 --> 00:19:23,770
She said, "I'm already busy, and now they're making me cook too?"

593
00:19:23,770 --> 00:19:25,100
She said something like...

594
00:19:25,100 --> 00:19:26,300
(Misunderstanding it would have been better.)

595
00:19:26,300 --> 00:19:27,770
She said something similar to that.

596
00:19:28,440 --> 00:19:29,940
Hold on a second.

597
00:19:29,940 --> 00:19:32,280
Wait, will I lose points for what I said?

598
00:19:32,280 --> 00:19:33,910
- With that attitude...
- You're eliminated.

599
00:19:34,380 --> 00:19:35,850
You're done for.

600
00:19:35,950 --> 00:19:37,880
With that mindset,

601
00:19:37,880 --> 00:19:39,680
- how can you cook?
- It's impossible.

602
00:19:39,680 --> 00:19:40,920
Food should be made with love.

603
00:19:40,920 --> 00:19:42,490
Is there anyone here...

604
00:19:42,490 --> 00:19:44,050
- who isn't busy?
- I have something to clarify.

605
00:19:44,050 --> 00:19:46,460
- What would you like to clarify?
- At that time,

606
00:19:46,460 --> 00:19:47,820
I was going out to eat.

607
00:19:47,820 --> 00:19:49,230
- Actually, I was on vacation.
- Right.

608
00:19:49,230 --> 00:19:50,390
I wasn't busy,

609
00:19:50,390 --> 00:19:52,930
- but Young Ji was busy...
- Let's go, Russian Roulette.

610
00:19:52,930 --> 00:19:54,530
because she had a concert.

611
00:19:54,530 --> 00:19:55,800
But I wasn't busy.

612
00:19:55,800 --> 00:19:57,670
It wasn't Yu Jin. It was Young Ji who...

613
00:19:57,670 --> 00:19:58,770
I really wasn't busy.

614
00:19:58,770 --> 00:20:01,770
I'll just say that Young Ji had a concert.

615
00:20:01,770 --> 00:20:03,070
Young Ji, please sit up.

616
00:20:03,070 --> 00:20:04,780
(Suddenly sitting up)

617
00:20:04,780 --> 00:20:06,580
- Either way...
- Personally,

618
00:20:06,580 --> 00:20:08,880
there's a reason why I feel deeply betrayed...

619
00:20:08,880 --> 00:20:11,520
- by this branch manager.
- He's a team leader.

620
00:20:11,520 --> 00:20:12,920
That day, we had a nice meal...

621
00:20:12,920 --> 00:20:15,890
- at an expensive restaurant.
- Right.

622
00:20:15,890 --> 00:20:17,150
We were his customers,

623
00:20:17,150 --> 00:20:18,860
and yet he accuses us of being gossipers.

624
00:20:18,990 --> 00:20:20,520
- Right.
- Gossipers.

625
00:20:20,520 --> 00:20:22,590
- You know what?
- We also played...

626
00:20:22,590 --> 00:20:24,660
a card picking game, and he picked my credit card.

627
00:20:24,660 --> 00:20:26,000
That's right.

628
00:20:26,000 --> 00:20:28,800
You were being very cheap at a fancy restaurant.

629
00:20:29,230 --> 00:20:30,730
At a fancy restaurant...

630
00:20:30,730 --> 00:20:32,700
- We made him pick a card.
- He picked my credit card.

631
00:20:32,700 --> 00:20:34,710
Do you have any special alliance with Mimi?

632
00:20:34,710 --> 00:20:36,070
Mimi and I...

633
00:20:36,070 --> 00:20:37,370
- You worked together before.
- We're...

634
00:20:37,370 --> 00:20:38,640
- best friends.
- Right, you have an advantage.

635
00:20:38,640 --> 00:20:40,410
That could raise questions about fairness.

636
00:20:40,410 --> 00:20:42,710
- Right. It's not fair at all.
- It makes me even more nervous.

637
00:20:42,710 --> 00:20:44,450
He judges me with complete objectivity.

638
00:20:44,450 --> 00:20:45,580
Of course.

639
00:20:45,580 --> 00:20:47,320
Haven't you met Eun Ji after the show...

640
00:20:47,320 --> 00:20:48,550
- as well?
- Yes, we met two times.

641
00:20:48,550 --> 00:20:50,590
We met that one time,

642
00:20:50,590 --> 00:20:51,820
but I don't even have his phone number.

643
00:20:51,820 --> 00:20:53,690
We don't have it either. Do you?

644
00:20:53,690 --> 00:20:55,230
- I guess she does.
- No, wait.

645
00:20:55,230 --> 00:20:56,460
- You got his business card.
- Wait.

646
00:20:56,460 --> 00:20:57,490
- Business card?
- You got his business card.

647
00:20:57,490 --> 00:20:58,730
I gave you my business card. Did you throw it away?

648
00:20:59,360 --> 00:21:00,830
If you got his business card,

649
00:21:00,830 --> 00:21:03,430
- you should've said hello.
- The business card...

650
00:21:03,430 --> 00:21:04,570
- Sit down, Young Ji.
- You got his business card.

651
00:21:04,570 --> 00:21:05,700
- She never contacted me.
- Sit back down.

652
00:21:05,700 --> 00:21:07,240
- Hurry, Young Ji.
- Speaking of business cards...

653
00:21:07,240 --> 00:21:08,710
Everyone has an Instagram account these days.

654
00:21:10,470 --> 00:21:12,240
- We follow each other on Instagram.
- Right.

655
00:21:12,240 --> 00:21:13,880
- You follow each other?
- Yes.

656
00:21:13,880 --> 00:21:15,180
Seriously?

657
00:21:15,180 --> 00:21:17,080
- What's the big deal?
- That's favoritism.

658
00:21:17,080 --> 00:21:18,980
- We follow each other.
- In this day and age,

659
00:21:18,980 --> 00:21:21,420
Instagram is a big deal. They even follow each other?

660
00:21:21,620 --> 00:21:23,820
I'll unfollow everyone including Yeong Seok.

661
00:21:24,150 --> 00:21:26,720
- Please keep following me.
- Okay, I will.

662
00:21:26,720 --> 00:21:27,890
Please evaluate strictly as you normally do.

663
00:21:27,890 --> 00:21:29,160
I'll be very strict.

664
00:21:29,160 --> 00:21:31,500
It's not that I know everyone personally.

665
00:21:31,500 --> 00:21:33,500
In the end, your relationship with everyone is vague.

666
00:21:33,500 --> 00:21:35,300
We aren't very close, but...

667
00:21:35,300 --> 00:21:36,330
(It turns out that he knows everyone quite equally.)

668
00:21:36,330 --> 00:21:38,070
- I'll be fair with everyone.
- Right.

669
00:21:38,070 --> 00:21:39,540
- I'll judge based on taste alone.
- Please do.

670
00:21:39,540 --> 00:21:40,770
- Evaluate based on taste alone.
- We'll do our best.

671
00:21:40,770 --> 00:21:42,570
Could you show us the kitchen for the competition?

672
00:21:42,570 --> 00:21:44,370
Let's go. Actually, it's my first time seeing it.

673
00:21:45,680 --> 00:21:48,150
Isn't he our first guest on "Earth Arcade?"

674
00:21:48,150 --> 00:21:49,180
I see.

675
00:21:50,050 --> 00:21:51,110
(He looks completely drained already.)

676
00:21:51,110 --> 00:21:52,580
He looks extremely uncomfortable.

677
00:21:52,750 --> 00:21:54,180
(Exclaiming)

678
00:21:54,180 --> 00:21:55,990
- This is it.
- This is so much pressure.

679
00:21:56,790 --> 00:21:59,620
(A competition kitchen designed to maximize the pressure)

680
00:21:59,760 --> 00:22:00,990
(Head Chef Selection for the 1st Earth Location)

681
00:22:00,990 --> 00:22:02,260
"Head Chef Selection."

682
00:22:02,260 --> 00:22:04,030
(The head chef to lead Space Rice Cake will be chosen here.)

683
00:22:04,030 --> 00:22:06,230
This place is no joke.

684
00:22:06,560 --> 00:22:07,560
(Who will become the winner?)

685
00:22:07,560 --> 00:22:09,270
Master Chef Korea.

686
00:22:11,100 --> 00:22:17,570
(Everyone sets out the rice cakes they brought.)

687
00:22:18,410 --> 00:22:19,780
We need to lay out all the ingredients.

688
00:22:19,780 --> 00:22:20,940
Get out of my way.

689
00:22:21,340 --> 00:22:22,780
- Why did everyone...
- Gosh, my back hurts.

690
00:22:22,950 --> 00:22:24,980
bring rice cakes?

691
00:22:24,980 --> 00:22:27,080
You didn't bring any? This is a rice cake competition.

692
00:22:27,450 --> 00:22:29,390
Mine are special rice cakes.

693
00:22:30,390 --> 00:22:31,860
What are special rice cakes?

694
00:22:32,060 --> 00:22:34,320
They're the kind that you can't find at rice cake shops.

695
00:22:34,390 --> 00:22:35,860
Do they have colors?

696
00:22:35,860 --> 00:22:37,030
(I won't tell you.)

697
00:22:37,090 --> 00:22:38,160
What are special rice cakes?

698
00:22:38,160 --> 00:22:39,460
(An eternal mystery)

699
00:22:39,660 --> 00:22:41,870
Once everyone is at their station,

700
00:22:41,870 --> 00:22:44,300
you can write your competition nickname in front of you.

701
00:22:44,300 --> 00:22:46,600
- In English?
- I will be called Neapolitan.

702
00:22:48,670 --> 00:22:49,740
"Neapolitan?"

703
00:22:50,470 --> 00:22:51,710
Neapolitan Tteokfia.

704
00:22:54,340 --> 00:22:55,750
Don't you dare use that name.

705
00:22:56,650 --> 00:22:57,810
"Neapolitan Tteokfia?"

706
00:22:57,950 --> 00:23:00,620
Since I like "Tazza," I'll be Monkfish Beast.

707
00:23:00,980 --> 00:23:03,590
- Eun Ji, that's not bad.
- Monkfish Beast.

708
00:23:03,750 --> 00:23:04,860
Then I will be...

709
00:23:05,660 --> 00:23:07,190
Mimokase.

710
00:23:08,860 --> 00:23:11,360
(Yu Jin starts off with a Michelin star.)

711
00:23:11,600 --> 00:23:13,960
If you're more or less ready...

712
00:23:13,960 --> 00:23:15,300
- No, not yet.
- Okay.

713
00:23:21,140 --> 00:23:22,970
Gosh, what's that?

714
00:23:24,240 --> 00:23:26,710
(What's that?)

715
00:23:26,880 --> 00:23:29,410
(A giant prop that instantly intimidates the others)

716
00:23:30,080 --> 00:23:31,880
(Young Ji who became a giant garaetteok...)

717
00:23:31,880 --> 00:23:33,680
(and a mysterious height scale next to her)

718
00:23:33,920 --> 00:23:36,820
(And the members' names)

719
00:23:37,850 --> 00:23:39,790
- There she goes again.
- It's for a performance.

720
