975
00:34:32,340 --> 00:34:36,150
I was desperately hoping for the cross section to turn out well.

976
00:34:36,450 --> 00:34:37,710
The cross section came out well.

977
00:34:39,120 --> 00:34:41,380
Personally, I'm satisfied.

978
00:34:41,980 --> 00:34:43,290
I could die happy.

979
00:34:44,650 --> 00:34:48,260
I was confused. It was always hard and exhausting,

980
00:34:49,290 --> 00:34:50,430
but this is my victory.

981
00:34:51,160 --> 00:34:52,260
The emotion,

982
00:34:54,200 --> 00:34:55,670
the homage,

983
00:34:56,670 --> 00:34:59,940
all of those elements are in this dish.

984
00:35:00,300 --> 00:35:01,540
The victory is mine.

985
00:35:02,740 --> 00:35:05,140
(A satisfied sigh)

986
00:35:05,510 --> 00:35:07,440
- What's this?
- Isn't it pretty?

987
00:35:07,440 --> 00:35:08,850
Eun Ji, this looks wonderful.

988
00:35:09,380 --> 00:35:12,050
(Humming sounds)

989
00:35:12,780 --> 00:35:14,880
(Playful music)

990
00:35:15,080 --> 00:35:16,320
Yu Jin, it looks like you have nothing much to do.

991
00:35:16,320 --> 00:35:17,350
That's not true.

992
00:35:18,220 --> 00:35:20,390
You could call it taking 1 step back to move 2 steps forward.

993
00:35:21,160 --> 00:35:24,890
(The sound of taking 2 steps forward and 1 step back)

994
00:35:25,060 --> 00:35:27,000
Didn't you only step back? Wait.

995
00:35:27,060 --> 00:35:30,730
(Visibly offended)

996
00:35:32,170 --> 00:35:33,200
Hello.

997
00:35:34,640 --> 00:35:35,770
This is An Sung Jin.

998
00:35:36,910 --> 00:35:38,940
You know that famous star chef?

999
00:35:38,940 --> 00:35:40,610
Is your nickname based on his name?

1000
00:35:41,540 --> 00:35:44,010
No, it's not. My name is An Sung Jin.

1001
00:35:44,510 --> 00:35:45,550
Right.

1002
00:35:45,950 --> 00:35:50,050
I'd describe my dish as Earth Arcade.

1003
00:35:50,250 --> 00:35:51,950
If you're a fan of "Earth Arcade,"

1004
00:35:51,950 --> 00:35:54,290
this is exactly the kind of dish you'd want to try.

1005
00:35:54,560 --> 00:35:57,490
- It captures the show's...
- It looks so good.

1006
00:35:57,490 --> 00:36:00,360
popularity and influence.

1007
00:36:00,860 --> 00:36:02,270
The dishes I made today are...

1008
00:36:02,700 --> 00:36:04,830
YJY tteokbokki...

1009
00:36:04,830 --> 00:36:06,300
and ex-boyfriend rice cake.

1010
00:36:07,240 --> 00:36:09,910
Last year's Earth Arcade Buldak became a huge hit.

1011
00:36:10,140 --> 00:36:13,280
That inspired me to turn it into a tteokbokki...

1012
00:36:13,280 --> 00:36:15,680
with noodle-shaped rice cakes.

1013
00:36:15,680 --> 00:36:17,680
(With noodle-shaped rice cakes)

1014
00:36:19,380 --> 00:36:21,080
(Special rice cakes that she bragged about earlier)

1015
00:36:21,080 --> 00:36:22,790
(Manufactured by a major food company)

1016
00:36:23,150 --> 00:36:24,820
I added sausages.

1017
00:36:25,150 --> 00:36:28,120
I replaced the egg yolk with boiled eggs.

1018
00:36:29,930 --> 00:36:31,690
Another huge trend last year was...

1019
00:36:31,690 --> 00:36:32,860
Thanks to Young Ji,

1020
00:36:32,860 --> 00:36:35,230
ex-boyfriend toast became a huge trend.

1021
00:36:35,230 --> 00:36:37,870
It even went viral on TikTok...

1022
00:36:37,870 --> 00:36:40,700
as ex-boyfriend toast.

1023
00:36:40,970 --> 00:36:44,510
Since we're aiming for a more global audience,

1024
00:36:44,670 --> 00:36:46,810
I wondered if I could reinterpret it in a different way.

1025
00:36:47,110 --> 00:36:49,880
So I replaced the toast with rice cake.

1026
00:36:50,410 --> 00:36:51,610
Doesn't it look fancy?

1027
00:36:52,680 --> 00:36:53,950
Is there anything I can taste?

1028
00:36:53,950 --> 00:36:54,950
- Taste?
- Yes.

1029
00:36:54,950 --> 00:36:56,090
- There is.
- There is something.

1030
00:36:56,190 --> 00:36:57,950
- Try a little. It can be spicy.
- Okay.

1031
00:37:04,130 --> 00:37:07,960
(The sound of fussing around)

1032
00:37:08,900 --> 00:37:11,670
(The sound of an unimpressed reaction)

1033
00:37:12,070 --> 00:37:13,270
What's the matter?

1034
00:37:16,270 --> 00:37:17,710
Yu Jin is...

1035
00:37:18,540 --> 00:37:20,080
a good cook.

1036
00:37:20,410 --> 00:37:21,640
She makes delicious food...

1037
00:37:21,780 --> 00:37:23,450
and gets the balance right.

1038
00:37:23,850 --> 00:37:24,910
However,

1039
00:37:25,680 --> 00:37:28,020
I think she played too safe.

1040
00:37:28,680 --> 00:37:30,690
Could you add something more?

1041
00:37:30,690 --> 00:37:31,720
(The sound of glaring)

1042
00:37:31,720 --> 00:37:33,490
Yu Jin kept glaring at me.

1043
00:37:34,660 --> 00:37:38,130
She looked at me with those crazy eyes. It was terrifying.

1044
00:37:39,130 --> 00:37:40,430
To be honest,

1045
00:37:41,460 --> 00:37:43,570
I didn't feel comfortable with winning first place.

1046
00:37:44,300 --> 00:37:47,770
I couldn't possibly tell the older girls what to do.

1047
00:37:47,770 --> 00:37:49,540
That would be so rude.

1048
00:37:49,910 --> 00:37:53,780
To follow the head chef's orders quietly,

1049
00:37:54,040 --> 00:37:55,680
I was aiming for second place.

1050
00:37:55,680 --> 00:37:56,750
I figured...

1051
00:37:57,750 --> 00:37:59,420
I'd be serving under the head chef.

1052
00:38:00,480 --> 00:38:02,750
Other than yourself, who do you think...

1053
00:38:02,890 --> 00:38:04,890
is the strongest contender?

1054
00:38:04,890 --> 00:38:06,090
- Other than myself?
- Yes.

1055
00:38:06,090 --> 00:38:07,190
It's An Yu Jin.

1056
00:38:07,190 --> 00:38:08,490
(Exhaling in thought)

1057
00:38:08,660 --> 00:38:13,330
Lately, she's been working with food a lot.

1058
00:38:14,130 --> 00:38:18,300
I'd say Kim Mi Hyun. She seems very competitive.

1059
00:38:18,470 --> 00:38:21,770
Rice cakes can be considered desserts.

1060
00:38:21,970 --> 00:38:23,440
When it comes to rice cake desserts,

1061
00:38:23,440 --> 00:38:26,810
who would surpass Mi Hyun?

1062
00:38:27,640 --> 00:38:28,840
Hello, everyone.

1063
00:38:29,150 --> 00:38:32,150
I'm here to become the head chef of Space Rice Cake.

1064
00:38:32,480 --> 00:38:33,620
This is Mimokase.

1065
00:38:33,620 --> 00:38:35,620
(The sound of showing off her beauty)

1066
00:38:35,850 --> 00:38:38,650
There's no grand concept behind my dishes.

1067
00:38:38,920 --> 00:38:41,320
Rice cakes can become pasta,

1068
00:38:41,320 --> 00:38:44,230
lasagna, or even tiramisu.

1069
00:38:44,690 --> 00:38:46,060
Rice cakes are all-purpose.

1070
00:38:46,500 --> 00:38:48,060
They're like a chameleon.

1071
00:38:48,460 --> 00:38:50,870
I just made three delicious dishes.

1072
00:38:52,030 --> 00:38:53,740
I wanted the texture...

1073
00:38:53,870 --> 00:38:55,670
- It's hot.
- to be nice and bouncy.

1074
00:38:55,840 --> 00:38:58,340
Then I thought about slicing up some jeolpyeon.

1075
00:38:58,340 --> 00:39:00,010
- Jeolpyeon has...
- Gosh, it's hot.

1076
00:39:00,010 --> 00:39:02,240
a much bouncier, chewier texture.

1077
00:39:02,340 --> 00:39:05,880
It'd be nice if I cut it to look like pasta.

1078
00:39:06,480 --> 00:39:08,150
I'll dump in every tasty ingredient...

1079
00:39:08,450 --> 00:39:10,550
and secure the first place.

1080
00:39:11,290 --> 00:39:12,560
(Manager Kwon is surprised.)

1081
00:39:13,920 --> 00:39:15,290
(Scanning the ingredients)

1082
00:39:15,290 --> 00:39:17,260
You nag way too much.

1083
00:39:18,030 --> 00:39:19,700
- Not bad, right?
- You're not making pasta, are you?

1084
00:39:20,830 --> 00:39:22,160
(Comical music plays.)

1085
00:39:22,500 --> 00:39:23,500
Come on, sir.

1086
00:39:23,500 --> 00:39:25,400
You're not going to replace pasta noodles with rice cakes...

1087
00:39:25,600 --> 00:39:27,670
and cook using a pasta recipe...

1088
00:39:28,540 --> 00:39:30,970
which already exists, right? Using cream and all later?

1089
00:39:31,670 --> 00:39:33,740
Why would you stir me up?

1090
00:39:33,810 --> 00:39:35,010
Isn't it just cream tteokbokki?

1091
00:39:35,680 --> 00:39:36,710
This is crazy.

1092
00:39:37,880 --> 00:39:39,520
Why are you so sensitive?

1093
00:39:40,120 --> 00:39:41,280
Do you have anything to say?

1094
00:39:41,380 --> 00:39:43,920
Please see me in a good light. You look so handsome today.

1095
00:39:44,120 --> 00:39:45,220
You look exceptionally handsome today.

1096
00:39:45,220 --> 00:39:46,260
- Right?
- Yes.

1097
00:39:46,390 --> 00:39:48,920
Your hair looks great today. Good job changing the part.

1098
00:39:49,990 --> 00:39:52,930
Chef Kwon has issues.

1099
00:39:53,300 --> 00:39:55,970
He makes you feel uncomfortable...

1100
00:39:56,300 --> 00:39:59,700
before he leaves.

1101
00:39:59,800 --> 00:40:01,940
I'm doing my best to cook,

1102
00:40:02,840 --> 00:40:04,510
and he'll silently lift one eyebrow.

1103
00:40:05,910 --> 00:40:07,080
He'll do this and walk away.

1104
00:40:07,080 --> 00:40:09,310
He makes you feel very nervous.

1105
00:40:09,850 --> 00:40:12,620
He is addicted to survival shows.

1106
00:40:13,180 --> 00:40:16,520
He enjoys the tension and the thrill of the final.

1107
00:40:17,590 --> 00:40:20,720
That's how it feels like. He has issues.

1108
00:40:22,690 --> 00:40:23,890
(The music to cue the start of her 3rd cooking)

1109
00:40:24,090 --> 00:40:27,230
Baekramisu. This is tteokramisu.

1110
00:40:27,860 --> 00:40:30,500
Tiramisu has biscuits in between.

1111
00:40:30,500 --> 00:40:31,970
Instead of the biscuits,

1112
00:40:32,740 --> 00:40:36,010
I'll be using baekseolgi.

1113
00:40:36,210 --> 00:40:39,010
The baekseolgi they sell is pretty thick,

1114
00:40:39,010 --> 00:40:40,910
So I'll slice it thinly into half,

1115
00:40:41,280 --> 00:40:42,750
cut it into 2 or 3 parts,

1116
00:40:42,750 --> 00:40:44,880
and pile the pieces up.

1117
00:40:45,750 --> 00:40:48,820
(Espresso)

1118
00:40:49,720 --> 00:40:52,320
Also, baekseolgi is one of the rice cakes...

1119
00:40:52,790 --> 00:40:54,490
which absorb liquid well.

1120
00:40:56,530 --> 00:40:57,590
(Mimokase crying out)

1121
00:40:57,730 --> 00:40:58,790
This isn't it.

1122
00:40:59,090 --> 00:41:00,730
(Tense music)

1123
00:41:01,200 --> 00:41:03,730
(Cream whipping sound)

1124
00:41:04,530 --> 00:41:05,600
Why is it so yellow?

1125
00:41:07,040 --> 00:41:09,410
If you were trying to make tiramisu, you've failed.

1126
00:41:09,410 --> 00:41:10,410
(Scoffing)

1127
00:41:10,410 --> 00:41:11,410
Is it not this cream?

1128
00:41:12,640 --> 00:41:14,810
- You have 17 minutes left.
- Understood!

1129
00:41:15,540 --> 00:41:17,380
Egg yolks.

1130
00:41:17,380 --> 00:41:18,410
(Mimokase poured in 4 egg yolks.)

1131
00:41:18,410 --> 00:41:19,820
(But...)

1132
00:41:19,920 --> 00:41:22,550
Actually, I never used all four when I practiced.

1133
00:41:22,550 --> 00:41:25,090
Today, I put in four because that's the right amount.

1134
00:41:25,190 --> 00:41:27,560
But it turned too yellow, so I added more whipped cream,

1135
00:41:27,560 --> 00:41:28,820
and it became too watery.

1136
00:41:28,820 --> 00:41:31,390
So I couldn't make the scream.

1137
00:41:31,590 --> 00:41:32,660
She means custard cream.

1138
00:41:32,730 --> 00:41:34,600
(Laughing)

1139
00:41:34,900 --> 00:41:39,270
(She fell into the whipped cream nightmare.)

1140
00:41:39,500 --> 00:41:43,040
(The sound of the upgraded equipment)

1141
00:41:43,410 --> 00:41:45,880
If you were trying to make tiramisu, you've failed.

1142
00:41:46,680 --> 00:41:47,680
Is it not this cream?

1143
00:41:47,680 --> 00:41:48,680
(The sound of failed cream)

1144
00:41:48,680 --> 00:41:50,110
- This...
- How did you make it?

1145
00:41:50,880 --> 00:41:52,150
Using my gut feeling.

1146
00:41:53,250 --> 00:41:55,920
Shall I give you a tip as a friend?

1147
00:41:56,820 --> 00:41:57,990
Did you use up mascarpone?

1148
00:41:57,990 --> 00:41:59,990
No, I have one left. I did add in more.

1149
00:41:59,990 --> 00:42:02,730
It will get thicker if you use mascarpone.

1150
00:42:03,130 --> 00:42:06,430
If you add it directly into this, it won't get thick enough.

1151
00:42:06,530 --> 00:42:08,800
So add half of the cream to mascarpone,

1152
00:42:08,800 --> 00:42:09,800
and it should get thicker.

1153
00:42:12,030 --> 00:42:14,070
- I'll tell you that much.
- Thank you, Mr. Kwon.

1154
00:42:14,370 --> 00:42:16,410
Chef Kwon Sung Jun...

1155
00:42:16,770 --> 00:42:19,740
is very good at wielding his carrot and stick.

1156
00:42:20,310 --> 00:42:21,510
So I hurriedly made it.

1157
00:42:25,480 --> 00:42:27,980
Actually, looking at their cooking...

1158
00:42:28,580 --> 00:42:29,750
made me lower my expectations.

1159
00:42:30,420 --> 00:42:34,660
(Manager Kwon Sung Jun's point of view)

1160
00:42:34,660 --> 00:42:35,690
It's hot.

1161
00:42:35,690 --> 00:42:39,090
(Manager Kwon Sung Jun's point of view)

1162
00:42:41,300 --> 00:42:42,500
Are you really going to open a restaurant?

1163
00:42:43,930 --> 00:42:45,600
- Why? Are you worried?
- I'm looking forward to it.

1164
00:42:45,600 --> 00:42:46,770
I want to go there too.

1165
00:42:47,140 --> 00:42:48,970
Weren't you coming with us?

1166
00:42:48,970 --> 00:42:50,610
Will my name be in the restaurant?

1167
00:42:51,970 --> 00:42:53,040
We'll put it up.

1168
00:42:53,510 --> 00:42:55,410
(Something worse than his name will be put up.)

1169
00:42:55,780 --> 00:42:57,050
You have 14 minutes left.

1170
00:42:57,510 --> 00:42:59,350
- This is crazy.
- That's more than enough time.

1171
00:42:59,350 --> 00:43:01,850
Let's finish this up.

1172
00:43:01,850 --> 00:43:02,920
(Dried pumpkin)

1173
00:43:04,090 --> 00:43:05,650
(Mimokase screams.)

1174
00:43:06,090 --> 00:43:07,120
This isn't...

1175
00:43:07,290 --> 00:43:09,730
I should've stir-fried dried pumpkin together with this.

1176
00:43:09,830 --> 00:43:11,130
(She loses her mind.)

1177
00:43:11,530 --> 00:43:13,160
It was too late to turn back.

1178
00:43:13,160 --> 00:43:14,800
I only remembered when I sliced the dried pumpkin.

1179
00:43:15,130 --> 00:43:16,830
It can't be helped.

1180
00:43:21,740 --> 00:43:25,070
Am I supposed to be doing this without cooking utensils?

1181
00:43:25,070 --> 00:43:26,310
(Smirking in dismay)

1182
00:43:26,680 --> 00:43:28,010
I need to make it sweet. Sugar.

1183
00:43:28,710 --> 00:43:30,510
- I have sugar.
- I have it too.

1184
00:43:30,680 --> 00:43:32,010
(Dish completed: 1. Neapolitan Tteokfia)

1185
00:43:32,010 --> 00:43:34,620
- Young Ji finished 1st.
- Young Ji finished 1st.

1186
00:43:35,080 --> 00:43:36,150
Time's almost up.

1187
00:43:36,150 --> 00:43:37,650
(2. An Sung Jin)

1188
00:43:37,650 --> 00:43:38,720
An Yu Jin is done.

1189
00:43:38,720 --> 00:43:39,720
(Mimokase)

1190
00:43:39,720 --> 00:43:40,920
(3. Mimokase)

1191
00:43:40,920 --> 00:43:42,090
Mimokase has finished.

1192
00:43:42,730 --> 00:43:45,160
- Done.
- Done.

1193
00:43:45,160 --> 00:43:46,400
Finish it quickly.

1194
00:43:46,730 --> 00:43:48,860
(The evaluation starts.)

1195
00:43:49,330 --> 00:43:52,100
- I shall start the presentation.
- Okay.

1196
00:43:52,300 --> 00:43:55,170
The name of this tteokbokki is "kiddie tteokbokki."

1197
00:43:55,170 --> 00:43:56,310
- Kiddie tteokbokki?
- Yes.

1198
00:43:57,010 --> 00:43:58,940
It brings back childhood memories, thus the name.

1199
00:44:00,210 --> 00:44:01,480
When you were an elementary school kid,

1200
00:44:01,480 --> 00:44:04,080
you had tteokbokki in front of a griddle.

1201
00:44:04,080 --> 00:44:06,450
It evokes nostalgia and tastes good,

1202
00:44:07,650 --> 00:44:09,820
but above all, it has the best turnover rate.

1203
00:44:09,820 --> 00:44:11,090
We'll be opening a restaurant.

1204
00:44:11,420 --> 00:44:12,860
If the turnover rate is good...

1205
00:44:13,620 --> 00:44:14,660
Yes, that's it.

1206
00:44:15,320 --> 00:44:17,890
But it looks...

1207
00:44:18,230 --> 00:44:21,130
(Tense music)

1208
00:44:21,330 --> 00:44:23,100
It looked...

1209
00:44:23,970 --> 00:44:26,300
rather unpleasant.

1210
00:44:28,870 --> 00:44:29,910
He ate it.

1211
00:44:30,710 --> 00:44:33,040
- Try the sausage too.
- How is it?

1212
00:44:33,040 --> 00:44:34,080
It must be good.

1213
00:44:34,280 --> 00:44:37,310
Young Ji added a lot of condiments to her food.

1214
00:44:37,910 --> 00:44:40,380
I was tempted by the condiments.

1215
00:44:41,280 --> 00:44:44,450
The taste of MSG and chicken stock wrapped around my tongue,

1216
00:44:45,020 --> 00:44:46,020
and it was hard to resist.

1217
00:44:47,320 --> 00:44:49,660
It must be tasty. It shows that he hasn't eaten.

1218
00:44:49,660 --> 00:44:51,130
He's on an empty stomach. That's what I was aiming for.

1219
00:44:51,130 --> 00:44:52,960
- It shows that he was hungry.
- You're lucky.

1220
00:44:52,960 --> 00:44:54,960
(Other chefs clap.)

1221
00:44:55,160 --> 00:44:56,770
Well, thank you.

1222
00:44:56,770 --> 00:44:58,730
- Kiddie tteokbokki.
- Follow me.

1223
00:44:59,200 --> 00:45:00,940
- My name is An Sung Jin.
- Hi.

1224
00:45:02,040 --> 00:45:03,070
This tteokbokki is...

1225
00:45:03,870 --> 00:45:05,940
"YJY tteokbokki."

1226
00:45:07,210 --> 00:45:09,340
Next, there's a toast which became very popular...

1227
00:45:09,340 --> 00:45:10,780
thanks to "Earth Arcade" last year.

1228
00:45:11,280 --> 00:45:12,920
Ex-boyfriend toast.

1229
00:45:12,920 --> 00:45:14,280
- Ex-boyfriend toast.
- It's ex-boyfriend toast.

1230
00:45:14,680 --> 00:45:16,120
- I made it go viral.
- Do you know about it?

1231
00:45:16,120 --> 00:45:17,490
- You copied it.
- It's all me.

1232
00:45:17,490 --> 00:45:18,820
I made the ex-boyfriend toast go viral.

1233
00:45:19,190 --> 00:45:22,020
That's why I named it YJY.

1234
00:45:22,020 --> 00:45:23,030
What does it stand for?

1235
00:45:23,030 --> 00:45:24,330
It's Yu Jin-Jae Young tteokbokki.

1236
00:45:24,430 --> 00:45:27,500
