- What?

1987
01:10:44,980 --> 01:10:46,910
It's Yu Jin from Season One.

1988
01:10:46,910 --> 01:10:47,980
She was like,

1989
01:10:47,980 --> 01:10:49,820
"You're not going to get your hair and makeup done, are you?"

1990
01:10:49,820 --> 01:10:51,550
Yu Jin from Season One is back.

1991
01:10:51,550 --> 01:10:53,250
- Hi.
- She does give off that vibe.

1992
01:10:53,250 --> 01:10:54,290
Hi.

1993
01:10:54,390 --> 01:10:57,520
I had a feeling today will be the only day I can look pretty.

1994
01:10:57,630 --> 01:10:59,630
- That's true.
- I also had the same feelings.

1995
01:10:59,630 --> 01:11:01,030
- You're not wrong, Mimi.
- Right?

1996
01:11:01,130 --> 01:11:02,830
(To the point as everyone is here)

1997
01:11:03,100 --> 01:11:04,830
Why are we here in the first place?

1998
01:11:04,830 --> 01:11:06,600
- Space fishing.
- Why are we at Space Service Area?

1999
01:11:06,600 --> 01:11:08,170
- Space Service Area.
- Our theme...

2000
01:11:08,170 --> 01:11:09,700
is a rice cake place in space.

2001
01:11:09,700 --> 01:11:12,140
Not many people know that theme.

2002
01:11:12,140 --> 01:11:15,010
What space? People think we just dance.

2003
01:11:15,010 --> 01:11:16,680
(This time, we're running a restaurant.)

2004
01:11:17,180 --> 01:11:19,450
We'll be heading to the place as a team...

2005
01:11:19,880 --> 01:11:21,180
- from here on out.
- Okay.

2006
01:11:21,180 --> 01:11:23,020
- Yu Jin is great at driving.
- What?

2007
01:11:23,580 --> 01:11:26,150
We prepared a car. It's over there.

2008
01:11:26,550 --> 01:11:27,990
- Is that why...
- You'll be taking that car...

2009
01:11:27,990 --> 01:11:29,420
as a team.

2010
01:11:29,420 --> 01:11:30,690
- No wonder we stopped...
- Follow my lead!

2011
01:11:30,690 --> 01:11:31,960
at a service area.

2012
01:11:31,960 --> 01:11:34,730
You're the head chef, while I'm the head driver.

2013
01:11:34,730 --> 01:11:36,230
- Right.
- We'll communicate through...

2014
01:11:36,230 --> 01:11:37,730
a walkie-talkie as we go.

2015
01:11:37,830 --> 01:11:39,670
Okie dokie Macintosh.

2016
01:11:39,670 --> 01:11:41,440
- Hold on.
- Calm down, Eun Ji.

2017
01:11:41,440 --> 01:11:43,900
- Please calm down.
- Keep your mannerism in check.

2018
01:11:43,900 --> 01:11:45,840
Her mannerism is already halfway there.

2019
01:11:45,840 --> 01:11:47,640
I'm already about to lose it.

2020
01:11:47,640 --> 01:11:50,540
You said I shouldn't let myself fall into a rut.

2021
01:11:50,540 --> 01:11:53,550
That's not mannerism. You're becoming self-deluded.

2022
01:11:53,650 --> 01:11:55,150
- It ends today.
- Right.

2023
01:11:55,380 --> 01:11:56,720
Here we go. Honesty.

2024
01:11:56,720 --> 01:11:58,420
- Humility. Akh!
- Humility. Akh!

2025
01:11:58,520 --> 01:12:00,320
(Getting in the car)

2026
01:12:01,460 --> 01:12:03,160
- I'm taking the passenger seat.
- What? No way.

2027
01:12:03,160 --> 01:12:04,460
- Isn't it a given?
- How is an unlicensed driver...

2028
01:12:04,460 --> 01:12:05,760
in the passenger seat?

2029
01:12:05,760 --> 01:12:08,530
- I've taken the driving test a lot.
- Young Ji.

2030
01:12:08,530 --> 01:12:10,560
- My bad.
- You don't have a license yet?

2031
01:12:10,560 --> 01:12:12,800
What's with that question? It's such an old one.

2032
01:12:12,800 --> 01:12:15,300
The guy I dated when I was 23 drove this car model.

2033
01:12:15,300 --> 01:12:16,370
All of a sudden?

2034
01:12:16,470 --> 01:12:18,710
So opening this back door made me recall those memories.

2035
01:12:18,710 --> 01:12:20,510
- Those moments were...
- Did you ride in the back?

2036
01:12:20,510 --> 01:12:21,710
Not in the front?

2037
01:12:22,410 --> 01:12:23,410
(A queen-like seat selection)

2038
01:12:23,410 --> 01:12:24,810
- Eun Ji is a queen at times.
- Exactly.

2039
01:12:24,810 --> 01:12:25,850
At times.

2040
01:12:26,480 --> 01:12:28,780
- Let's go, ma'am.
- Give me a minute.

2041
01:12:28,780 --> 01:12:31,050
- Okay.
- Where's the stick shift?

2042
01:12:31,620 --> 01:12:33,090
- Here it is.
- Is your seatbelt on?

2043
01:12:33,090 --> 01:12:34,120
Of course.

2044
01:12:34,120 --> 01:12:35,190
With a pretty outfit.

2045
01:12:35,190 --> 01:12:38,960
(Off to open the restaurant)

2046
01:12:39,290 --> 01:12:40,590
- Head Chef.
- Yes?

2047
01:12:40,590 --> 01:12:42,330
- Rumors have it that...
- Rumors have it that?

2048
01:12:42,330 --> 01:12:44,700
there's an actual real head chef.

2049
01:12:44,700 --> 01:12:46,430
What nonsense is that out of the blue?

2050
01:12:46,530 --> 01:12:49,800
I heard the head chef couldn't cook...

2051
01:12:49,800 --> 01:12:52,470
unless Mimi was next to her.

2052
01:12:52,470 --> 01:12:54,370
Director Ye Seul, you said some weird things to Eun Ji, didn't you?

2053
01:12:55,780 --> 01:12:58,010
Eun Ji thinks the head chef is Mimi.

2054
01:12:58,510 --> 01:12:59,510
What's going on?

2055
01:12:59,680 --> 01:13:01,120
(Laughing)

2056
01:13:01,580 --> 01:13:04,150
You're right, but only half right.

2057
01:13:04,850 --> 01:13:07,620
Mimi is something like a Dutch wife to me.

2058
01:13:08,220 --> 01:13:10,420
- A comfort toy?
- Yes, a talking Dutch wife.

2059
01:13:10,420 --> 01:13:11,490
- A comfort Dutch wife.
- A comfort Dutch wife.

2060
01:13:11,490 --> 01:13:12,530
Nice.

2061
01:13:12,530 --> 01:13:14,090
I'm overwhelmed with concerns.

2062
01:13:14,090 --> 01:13:16,160
An Yu Jin won't be able to act all pretty. Are you fine with it?

2063
01:13:16,730 --> 01:13:18,070
- I'm sure that's what you think.
- Giving up...

2064
01:13:18,930 --> 01:13:20,930
However, one clip while cutting the radish.

2065
01:13:21,030 --> 01:13:22,170
One clip while cutting the spring onion.

2066
01:13:22,600 --> 01:13:23,600
Look forward to it.

2067
01:13:23,600 --> 01:13:24,970
By the way, how are you this good...

2068
01:13:24,970 --> 01:13:26,340
- at driving, Yu Jin?
- I know, right?

2069
01:13:26,340 --> 01:13:28,840
- It's super smooth.
- Is that so? I'm glad.

2070
01:13:28,840 --> 01:13:29,880
I get nervous...

2071
01:13:29,880 --> 01:13:30,910
- when it's a full car.
- Is that so?

2072
01:13:31,180 --> 01:13:33,550
- Are you nervous?
- Yes, the car is full.

2073
01:13:34,680 --> 01:13:37,820
I'm dead nervous. I've never been this nervous during "Earth Arcade."

2074
01:13:38,290 --> 01:13:41,220
Young Ji has that Joan of Arc-like quality.

2075
01:13:41,220 --> 01:13:43,290
- Yes.
- The quality...

2076
01:13:43,290 --> 01:13:44,990
- Exactly.
- of a female leader.

2077
01:13:44,990 --> 01:13:47,360
That title of yours is what makes the show...

2078
01:13:47,590 --> 01:13:49,500
- I agree.
- much better in quality.

2079
01:13:49,500 --> 01:13:51,700
- A little bit of pressure.
- A little bit of mannerism.

2080
01:13:51,800 --> 01:13:53,930
A little bit of dead spirit. A little bit of low self-esteem.

2081
01:13:54,800 --> 01:13:56,300
- A little bit of nosebleed.
- A little bit of nosebleed.

2082
01:13:56,540 --> 01:13:59,440
- We need a part-time worker.
- A part-time worker?

2083
01:13:59,870 --> 01:14:01,780
I bet we'll fight if one is hired.

2084
01:14:01,880 --> 01:14:03,410
Sorry to cut you off, but this isn't UFC.

2085
01:14:03,410 --> 01:14:05,450
Why have you been thinking we'd fight?

2086
01:14:05,450 --> 01:14:06,850
Why? Why do you think we'll fight?

2087
01:14:06,850 --> 01:14:08,450
As I was born...

2088
01:14:08,450 --> 01:14:11,450
with a brain that can only think of one thing at a time,

2089
01:14:11,750 --> 01:14:13,150
I can't multitask.

2090
01:14:13,150 --> 01:14:14,220
Wouldn't fighting with gentle words...

2091
01:14:14,220 --> 01:14:16,060
- Gentle words.
- be fine?

2092
01:14:16,320 --> 01:14:17,690
Let's simulate, Eun Ji.

2093
01:14:17,690 --> 01:14:19,230
- How?
- Eun Ji, I told you...

2094
01:14:19,230 --> 01:14:20,730
the red tteokbokki was for table three.

2095
01:14:20,730 --> 01:14:22,260
You said jjajang tteokbokki!

2096
01:14:23,000 --> 01:14:24,030
You wouldn't act like that...

2097
01:14:24,030 --> 01:14:25,470
- in the first place.
- She sounded like a mom.

2098
01:14:25,470 --> 01:14:26,900
- Stop pretending.
- Wait. Is that how you'll act...

2099
01:14:26,900 --> 01:14:27,900
in front of customers?

2100
01:14:27,900 --> 01:14:30,440
Exactly. You won't, will you?

2101
01:14:30,940 --> 01:14:34,440
(They will.)

2102
01:14:34,940 --> 01:14:36,110
I wonder...

2103
01:14:36,110 --> 01:14:37,480
- what the restaurant looks like.
- Same here.

2104
01:14:38,950 --> 01:14:40,010
I imagined it to be...

2105
01:14:40,010 --> 01:14:41,250
I bet it'll be pretty.

2106
01:14:41,750 --> 01:14:43,720
- A Korean vibe.
- Yes.

2107
01:14:43,720 --> 01:14:44,920
(The woods grow increasingly lush.)

2108
01:14:44,920 --> 01:14:46,090
Amazing.

2109
01:14:46,090 --> 01:14:47,650
(The woods grow increasingly lush.)

2110
01:14:48,090 --> 01:14:49,090
Yes!

2111
01:14:52,030 --> 01:14:54,060
- Stop it.
- Yes!

2112
01:14:54,060 --> 01:14:55,060
Yes!

2113
01:14:55,060 --> 01:14:56,160
(A commute that leaves them in awe)

2114
01:14:56,360 --> 01:14:57,870
Let's get a "yes" version...

2115
01:14:57,870 --> 01:14:58,870
- for each one.
- Okay.

2116
01:14:58,870 --> 01:15:00,430
- I'll go first.
- Starting with Young Ji.

2117
01:15:01,030 --> 01:15:02,070
(Shocked)

2118
01:15:02,070 --> 01:15:03,140
- What is that?
- What?

2119
01:15:03,140 --> 01:15:05,110
- We're here.
- Hey, that Torong.

2120
01:15:05,110 --> 01:15:06,970
I have a feeling we'll get a ton of customers.

2121
01:15:06,970 --> 01:15:08,310
Are you ready to slap Torong?

2122
01:15:08,310 --> 01:15:10,110
- It's a lot more...
- Why slap Torong?

2123
01:15:10,740 --> 01:15:12,380
- Why do we slap him?
- It's so pretty.

2124
01:15:12,380 --> 01:15:14,450
- I love it.
- Yes, it's pretty.

2125
01:15:15,980 --> 01:15:19,050
(A dazzling sea ahead)

2126
01:15:19,920 --> 01:15:24,260
(Lush pine trees on the side offer a place to rest.)

2127
01:15:25,090 --> 01:15:27,960
(A place to call home)

2128
01:15:27,960 --> 01:15:31,430
(A place to take a peaceful rest)

2129
01:15:31,630 --> 01:15:33,030
(Space Rice Cake)

2130
01:15:33,030 --> 01:15:35,040
(Space Rice Cake's first Earth location has opened...)

2131
01:15:35,040 --> 01:15:37,040
(in this heartwarming seaside village.)

2132
01:15:37,740 --> 01:15:42,880
(Welcome!)

2133
01:15:43,680 --> 01:15:44,710
- Thank you.
- No problem.

2134
01:15:44,710 --> 01:15:46,250
Torong!

2135
01:15:46,250 --> 01:15:47,350
Torong.

2136
01:15:47,680 --> 01:15:48,920
- Torong.
- Cheolbong.

2137
01:15:49,380 --> 01:15:50,520
- Cheolyong.
- Cheolyong.

2138
01:15:50,520 --> 01:15:52,190
Who is Cheolbong?

2139
01:15:52,390 --> 01:15:55,360
- Cheolyong has lost weight.
- Is that so?

2140
01:15:55,360 --> 01:15:56,420
Are you Longlong now?

2141
01:15:57,290 --> 01:15:59,330
Can you turn this off? It's distracting.

2142
01:16:00,490 --> 01:16:02,130
- Hi.
- It's even noisy.

2143
01:16:02,130 --> 01:16:04,770
Since it'll be your first shop,

2144
01:16:04,770 --> 01:16:06,230
let's have a ribbon-cutting ceremony...

2145
01:16:06,230 --> 01:16:07,670
- and take a commemorative photo.
- For real?

2146
01:16:07,770 --> 01:16:10,470
(A grand opening with all the essentials)

2147
01:16:11,270 --> 01:16:12,810
Guys, we're really about to open.

2148
01:16:12,810 --> 01:16:14,370
- Right?
- Whatever.

2149
01:16:14,370 --> 01:16:15,410
It's okay. We can do it.

2150
01:16:15,410 --> 01:16:17,210
Wait. Please say a word, Head Chef.

2151
01:16:17,910 --> 01:16:21,250
I'm grateful to begin a prosperous 2026,

2152
01:16:21,250 --> 01:16:23,650
the Year of the Horse,

2153
01:16:23,950 --> 01:16:25,390
- with my beloved family.
- Good.

2154
01:16:25,390 --> 01:16:26,950
Citizens of Goheung,

2155
01:16:27,820 --> 01:16:31,220
come have tteokbokki!

2156
01:16:31,530 --> 01:16:32,690
(A neck injury)

2157
01:16:32,690 --> 01:16:34,460
Are we using that speech just now?

2158
01:16:34,460 --> 01:16:37,100
- When I count to three...
- Torong just closed his ears.

2159
01:16:38,270 --> 01:16:39,900
When I count to three, we say "Ahk!"

2160
01:16:40,130 --> 01:16:41,200
Okay, honesty!

2161
01:16:41,200 --> 01:16:42,270
- Humility!
- Humility!

2162
01:16:42,270 --> 01:16:43,700
In 1, 2, 3.

2163
01:16:43,700 --> 01:16:45,570
- Ahk!
- Ahk!

2164
01:16:45,810 --> 01:16:48,210
(Everyone cuts the ribbon without a problem.)

2165
01:16:48,440 --> 01:16:49,810
Hers didn't cut.

2166
01:16:50,380 --> 01:16:52,250
- Why did... How come?
- It's okay.

2167
01:16:53,210 --> 01:16:54,280
What...

2168
01:16:54,820 --> 01:16:56,550
- Guys, the scissors...
- It's okay.

2169
01:16:57,120 --> 01:16:58,450
It's okay. We can do it.

2170
01:16:58,790 --> 01:17:00,520
- I'm taking the photo.
- Okay.

2171
01:17:00,520 --> 01:17:02,990
- Yes!
- Yes!

2172
01:17:02,990 --> 01:17:04,060
Yes!

2173
01:17:04,420 --> 01:17:06,760
- Is that a show-friendly word?
- I don't know.

2174
01:17:07,960 --> 01:17:09,760
Look at Chang Dae.

2175
01:17:11,200 --> 01:17:13,330
(A grand opening ceremony that feels a little off)

2176
01:17:14,430 --> 01:17:15,440
Chang Dae!

2177
01:17:15,440 --> 01:17:19,070
(What will happen to the Earth Arcaders?)

2178
01:17:19,570 --> 01:17:20,640
- Good. Thank you.
- Thank you.

2179
01:17:20,640 --> 01:17:21,680
Can we take a look?

2180
01:17:21,680 --> 01:17:23,810
- Yes, that's the restaurant.
- Take that entrance over there.

2181
01:17:24,180 --> 01:17:26,150
It does give off old store vibes.

2182
01:17:26,350 --> 01:17:27,880
Really, it's giving old store vibes.

2183
01:17:27,880 --> 01:17:28,920
- Oh, my gosh.
- What is it?

2184
01:17:29,320 --> 01:17:31,550
- How pretty.
- The place is so pretty.

2185
01:17:31,550 --> 01:17:34,120
Tteokbokki where you can see the sea ahead!

2186
01:17:34,120 --> 01:17:36,590
- It's so pretty.
- Tteokbokki where you can see...

2187
01:17:36,590 --> 01:17:37,760
the sea ahead!

2188
01:17:38,060 --> 01:17:39,930
- The kitchen is huge.
- It's seriously nice.

2189
01:17:40,030 --> 01:17:42,160
- It's nice.
- It is, right?

2190
01:17:42,160 --> 01:17:43,230
Oh, gosh.

2191
01:17:43,230 --> 01:17:44,700
- Is this the plate?
- Four each.

2192
01:17:44,700 --> 01:17:46,470
Tteokbokki where you can see the sea ahead, okay?

2193
01:17:46,470 --> 01:17:47,730
- Tteokbokki where you can see...
- Tteokbokki where you can see...

2194
01:17:47,730 --> 01:17:49,000
- the sea ahead!
- the sea ahead!

2195
01:17:49,000 --> 01:17:50,000
(Mysterious machines can be seen.)

2196
01:17:51,270 --> 01:17:53,470
(What are they for?)

2197
01:17:53,870 --> 01:17:56,080
(Their happiness doesn't last long.)

2198
01:17:56,410 --> 01:17:57,810
Hold on, Head Chef.

2199
01:17:57,810 --> 01:17:59,250
- I'm genuinely shocked.
- Yes?

2200
01:17:59,580 --> 01:18:00,650
We weren't told about making rice cakes.

2201
01:18:00,650 --> 01:18:02,680
If we have to run the rice cake dough through the machine too,

2202
01:18:02,680 --> 01:18:04,050
then seriously,

2203
01:18:04,050 --> 01:18:05,590
I'm not even joking when I say this,

2204
01:18:05,590 --> 01:18:06,620
but we're...

2205
01:18:07,220 --> 01:18:08,620
- Doomed?
- doomed.

2206
01:18:09,520 --> 01:18:12,390
(Misfortune runs deep and is relentless.)

2207
01:18:14,590 --> 01:18:16,360
So are we a tteokbokki place,

2208
01:18:16,360 --> 01:18:18,130
or a rice cake mill?

2209
01:18:18,300 --> 01:18:20,370
Honestly, I'm going insane.

2210
01:18:21,130 --> 01:18:22,840
Can't we just buy the rice cakes?

2211
01:18:23,900 --> 01:18:25,710
Gosh, why is this not working?

2212
01:18:27,210 --> 01:18:29,140
I think people first came up with swear words...

2213
01:18:29,640 --> 01:18:31,810
- while they were working.
- Of course.

2214
01:18:35,120 --> 01:18:36,880
So this is what running a business is like.

2215
01:18:38,720 --> 01:18:39,950
Who said I wanted to make rice cakes from scratch?

2216
01:18:40,220 --> 01:18:42,720
I never wanted to make rice cakes from scratch.

2217
01:18:42,720 --> 01:18:45,130
I just wanted to look cool cutting the rice cakes from the machine.

2218
01:18:45,130 --> 01:18:46,430
I never said I wanted to make baekseolgi from scratch...

2219
01:18:46,430 --> 01:18:47,730
and grind powder on top of it.

2220
01:18:47,730 --> 01:18:48,730
When have I ever said that?

2221
01:18:49,500 --> 01:18:51,900
No one better leave their rice cakes unfinished.

2222
01:18:52,500 --> 01:18:54,330
Yu Jin, write down the names of people who don't finish...

2223
01:18:54,330 --> 01:18:55,670
- the rice cakes and blacklist them.
- Okay.

2224
01:18:56,000 --> 01:18:57,970
(Coming soon: The brutal rice cake making)

2225
01:18:57,970 --> 01:18:59,910
(Coming up next)

2226
01:19:00,010 --> 01:19:03,010
(The secret weapon of Space Rice Cake)

2227
01:19:03,010 --> 01:19:06,950
(Freshly pulled, warm rice cakes)

2228
01:19:07,250 --> 01:19:10,580
(Most importantly, we need to focus on the rice cakes.)

2229
01:19:10,850 --> 01:19:12,590
(Jebyeong, what's wrong with you?)

2230
01:19:12,990 --> 01:19:14,190
(What's wrong with the machine?)

2231
01:19:14,190 --> 01:19:17,020
(The rice cake isn't coming out at all.)

2232
01:19:17,660 --> 01:19:19,190
(Why do the rice cakes...)

2233
01:19:19,190 --> 01:19:20,490
(look weird today?)

2234
01:19:20,560 --> 01:19:23,460
(From wrestling with garaetteok...)

2235
01:19:23,800 --> 01:19:24,930
(Pounding)

2236
01:19:24,930 --> 01:19:27,030
(to battling baekseolgi)

2237
01:19:27,170 --> 01:19:28,300
(Are you okay?)

2238
01:19:28,800 --> 01:19:29,840
(Yes.)

2239
01:19:29,840 --> 01:19:32,040
(A sticky battle of wills with rice cakes)

2240
01:19:32,240 --> 01:19:34,310
(But this was just the beginning.)

2241
01:19:35,110 --> 01:19:36,110
(Goodness, it's raining.)

2242
01:19:36,110 --> 01:19:37,180
(Is this really happening?)

2243
01:19:37,780 --> 01:19:40,080
(It's not Space Rice Cake anymore. It's Showers of Rain Rice Cake.)

2244
01:19:40,310 --> 01:19:42,620
(We haven't even started the business yet.)

2245
01:19:42,720 --> 01:19:44,480
(The floor is covered in water.)

2246
01:19:44,480 --> 01:19:47,290
(They're facing a flooding crisis.)

2247
01:19:47,490 --> 01:19:49,690
(We're a rice cake shop!)

2248
01:19:50,220 --> 01:19:51,760
(Please visit us!)

2249
01:19:52,060 --> 01:19:56,760
(Nothing is going right. Not the rice cakes, not the rain.)

2250
01:19:57,960 --> 01:19:59,430
(On top of that,)

2251
01:19:59,970 --> 01:20:02,570
(the streets are deserted.)

2252
01:20:02,870 --> 01:20:04,500
(This can't go on like this.)

2253
01:20:04,600 --> 01:20:07,770
(Plan 1: Putting on a promotional performance)

2254
01:20:07,770 --> 01:20:09,180
(The grand opening of Space Rice Cake)

2255
01:20:09,180 --> 01:20:10,540
(Please show us some love!)

2256
01:20:10,540 --> 01:20:11,650
(Show us some love!)

2257
01:20:11,650 --> 01:20:12,650
(Gosh, this is tasty!)

2258
01:20:12,650 --> 01:20:13,710
(This tteokbokki is so good!)

2259
01:20:13,710 --> 01:20:15,020
Where did you get this?

2260
01:20:15,350 --> 01:20:18,220
(Plan 2: Starting a self-fulfilling rumor)

2261
01:20:18,250 --> 01:20:20,650
(Excuse me, directors. Could just one of you stay here...)

2262
01:20:20,650 --> 01:20:22,220
(while the other three go out and help spread the word?)

2263
01:20:22,220 --> 01:20:24,290
(Plan 3: Bringing in outside help)

2264
01:20:26,590 --> 01:20:27,930
(You're our very first customer.)

2265
01:20:27,930 --> 01:20:30,230
(Customers start trickling in.)

2266
01:20:30,230 --> 01:20:33,200
(A wave of customers...)

2267
01:20:33,200 --> 01:20:35,340
(and a rush of orders)

2268
01:20:35,340 --> 01:20:37,240
(This is so different from what we expected.)

2269
01:20:37,240 --> 01:20:39,610
(The kitchen team has lost their minds.)

2270
01:20:39,610 --> 01:20:41,610
(Apparently, the pollock roe and clam pasta...)

2271
01:20:41,610 --> 01:20:42,680
(was served to another table.)

2272
01:20:42,680 --> 01:20:44,640
(Even the service team starts making mistakes?)

2273
01:20:47,080 --> 01:20:52,020
(What will become of Space Rice Cake amid all this chaos?)

2274
01:20:58,690 --> 01:21:00,030
(Space Rice Cake)

2275
01:21:00,560 --> 01:21:02,760
(Space Rice Cake)
